From d7b42db02cc74473bc175d2c37dd6feba1a77811 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:43:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: weigh one weapon in the blows calculation

borg_calc_blows() multiplied the weapon's weight by the stack size,
while the engine's calc_blows() weighs a single weapon.  For the
wielded weapon the two agree (quantity one), but for a stack of
weapons in the home the Borg's home-damage total used the whole
stack's weight, so a stack of light weapons was treated as one very
heavy weapon and under-counted the blows - measured natively at 1
blow versus the engine's 2 for a stack of ten rapiers.  Weigh one
weapon, like the engine.

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-trait.c b/src/borg/borg-trait.c
index 154eb3849..72904f742 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-trait.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-trait.c
@@ -1039,7 +1039,9 @@ int borg_calc_blows(borg_item *item)
     int div;
     int blow_energy;
 
-    int weight     = item->weight * item->iqty;
+    /* The engine weighs one weapon (object_weight_one): blows per
+     * weapon must not depend on how many weapons are stacked. */
+    int weight     = item->weight;
     int min_weight = player->class->min_weight;
 
     /* Enforce a minimum "weight" (tenth pounds) */
